# Operator words

Meat Bags run this at a desk. Buttons, copied URLs, HTTP paths, event `action`, and status lines use the **same two verbs**.

| Do this | Say this | HTTP |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Start or retrigger one slot | **Fire** | `GET\|POST /api/popup/{id}` |
| Take one slot down | **Stop** | `GET\|POST /api/popup/{id}/stop` |
| Start every enabled top-level slot | **Fire all** | fire each id (Ada sample on operator chrome) |
| Panic clear | **Stop all** | `GET\|POST /api/popup/stop_all` |

Composer **Test** is Fire with sample `{user}`=Ada. The composer plot **eye** is enable/disable, not Fire/Stop.

## Do not

- Mix families on one surface: Hide next to Stop all, Show all as the opposite of Stop all, Play vs Fire.
- A chameleon button that swaps **Show** / **Hide** / **Stop** by state. Labels stay **Fire** and **Stop**. Two actions, two buttons.
- Synonyms for the same job (`hide`, `unhide`, `panic`, `clear` on chrome). Overlay WS `show` / `stop` / `clear` maps Fire / Stop / Stop all — do not invent a fourth word on the operator page.
- Toggle copy as “copy hide URL” when the route is `/stop`.

Alpha: rename the path; no `/hide` alias.
